# FoodProof — server-only environment (phase-one invited demo)
# Copy to .env.local and fill with values from your DEMO Supabase/Mixpanel projects.
# Never commit real values. Never prefix a secret with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# Validation rules are enforced in lib/server/env.ts (see comments per var).

# --- Supabase (dedicated DEMO project; the secret key bypasses RLS, keep server-only) ---
# SUPABASE_URL: required, must be a valid https URL.
SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY: required, non-empty. The project's secret key
# (server-only; bypasses RLS). Never sent to the browser; never NEXT_PUBLIC_.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# --- Mixpanel (dedicated DEMO project; server proxy only) ---
# MIXPANEL_TOKEN: required, non-empty.
MIXPANEL_TOKEN=
# MIXPANEL_API_HOST: required, valid https URL for your data region (e.g. https://api-eu.mixpanel.com).
MIXPANEL_API_HOST=
# ANALYTICS_AUDIENCE: optional; "qa" or "invited_pilot" (default "invited_pilot").
# The `audience` envelope property that separates developer/QA traffic from
# invited testers (FOODPROOF_MEASUREMENT_AND_PILOT.md §1/§3 — "set by
# deployment/test session configuration"; §5 filters reports to
# audience=invited_pilot). Set it to "qa" in local and test environments; leave
# it unset (or "invited_pilot") on the deployment testers actually use. An
# invalid value is a startup error, never a silent fallback.
ANALYTICS_AUDIENCE=

# --- Application ---
# APP_ORIGIN: required, valid https URL of the deployed origin (used for same-origin checks).
APP_ORIGIN=
# RATE_LIMIT_HMAC_KEY: required, high-entropy secret keying the invitation-attempt limiter HMAC.
RATE_LIMIT_HMAC_KEY=
# DEMO_MODE: required, must be the literal string "true" in phase one.
DEMO_MODE=true

# --- AI (optional; assisted label extraction and complaint drafting) ---
# All three are optional. With AI_PROVIDER or AI_PROVIDER_API_KEY missing or
# blank, lib/server/ai.ts getAiAdapter() returns null, the two /ai routes answer
# DEPENDENCY_UNAVAILABLE ("AI assistance is unavailable.") and the mandatory
# manual / deterministic-template path keeps working exactly as before. The
# handoff documents in docs/ stay provider-neutral on purpose; this file is the
# operator's own configuration, so it may name the provider the owner chose.
#
# AI_PROVIDER: the only recognised value is "anthropic". Anything else — or blank
# — leaves the AI path switched off.
AI_PROVIDER=
# AI_PROVIDER_API_KEY: the provider API key. Server-only, never NEXT_PUBLIC_, and
# read only through lib/server/env.ts: the provider SDK is deliberately never
# allowed to pick up a key from its own environment lookup.
AI_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
# AI_MODEL: optional pinned model id. Default when unset: claude-sonnet-5. The id
# must have a price row in lib/server/ai/limits.ts (PRICED_MODELS) so the spend
# ledger can meter it; an unpriced id switches the AI path off with a logged
# reason rather than under-counting against the pilot cap.
AI_MODEL=

# OFFICIAL_PORTAL_KEY: optional. Names ONE allowlisted government destination key
# from lib/server/official.ts (the verified URL lives there in code, not here).
# The only recognised key today is "fssai_foscos_grievance" (the FSSAI Food Safety
# Connect consumer grievance portal, hand-verified). Unset, blank, or an unknown
# key leaves the reporter's "Open official portal" action disabled — never opening
# an unvetted URL. Set it only after re-verifying the destination (T5, A.3).
OFFICIAL_PORTAL_KEY=

# --- Email sign-in (phase two, C.1; docs/FOODPROOF_DECISIONS.md D18) ---
# EMAIL_SIGN_IN: optional. Only the literal string "true" enables it. It adds an
# email one-time-code sign-in path ALONGSIDE invitation-code entry; invitation
# entry keeps working unchanged and a verified account never claims a demo
# actor's records. Leave it unset for a phase-one deployment. Enabling it
# requires SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY below and migration 0006 applied to the
# project (see docs/FOODPROOF_SETUP_AND_OPERATIONS.md); a missing key is a
# startup error, not a runtime surprise.
EMAIL_SIGN_IN=
# MODERATOR_EMAILS: optional, comma-separated. The reviewer allowlist for
# VERIFIED accounts only — there is no role table. An address here signs in as a
# reviewer; removing it demotes that account on its next request. Case and
# surrounding spaces do not matter; an entry that is not an address is ignored.
# Invitation actors are unaffected: their role comes from their invitation.
MODERATOR_EMAILS=

# --- Supabase publishable key (test-only in phase one; required for C.1) ---
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY: the DEMO project's publishable key
# (sb_publishable_...), the key a browser would hold.
# Two uses, both server-side:
#   1. Tests: the direct-client denial test in tests/integration/boundary.test.ts
#      proves that a caller holding only this key is refused every table, RPC and
#      Storage operation. Without it that group is SKIPPED with a stated reason;
#      it never counts as a pass.
#   2. Email sign-in (EMAIL_SIGN_IN=true): the server builds a PER-REQUEST auth
#      client from it to send and verify one-time codes, so a user's provider
#      token never touches the service client.
# It is read through lib/server/env.ts, is never sent to the browser by this
# application, and is never prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_.
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
